# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local development (Postgres on your machine)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy to `.env`. Prisma reads this file for CLI commands (migrate, studio).
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/in_the_kitchen?schema=public"

# Optional: override demo user password when running `pnpm db:seed`
# DEMO_USER_PASSWORD="demo1234"

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase + Vercel (single variable — simplest)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Prisma only reads DATABASE_URL. Set this in Vercel → Settings → Environment Variables.
#
# Recommended for this app on Vercel: Supabase **Session pooler** (port 5432) + connection limit:
#
# DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres.[PROJECT-REF]:[PASSWORD]@aws-0-[REGION].pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres?connection_limit=1"
#
# Get the URI from Supabase → Connect → Session mode.
#
# Advanced (optional): Supabase docs also describe a **Transaction** pooler (6543) with
# `?pgbouncer=true&connection_limit=1` for heavy serverless; that needs a separate migration URL.
# This repo uses one DATABASE_URL only — use Session pooler unless you add `directUrl` back in schema.prisma.
#
# Prisma + Supabase: https://supabase.com/docs/guides/database/prisma

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vercel
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Add DATABASE_URL for Production (and Preview if needed), then redeploy.
# On Vercel (`VERCEL=1`) the build runs `prisma migrate deploy` then `next build` (scripts/build.mjs).
# Locally, `pnpm build` runs `next build` only.
#
# If the build fails with Prisma P1012 "Environment variable not found: DATABASE_URL":
#   - The variable is missing OR not enabled for the environment that is building.
#   - In Vercel env UI, open DATABASE_URL and ensure "Production" is checked (not only "Development").
#   - Preview deployments need "Preview" checked if you use preview branches.
#
# One-time from your machine (same DATABASE_URL in .env):
#   pnpm db:seed
#
# Verify: https://<your-domain>/api/health — expect ok: true, dbReachable: true.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Admin bootstrap (production)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Comma-separated emails that are upgraded to ADMIN on sign-in or sign-up.
# On Vercel: name is exactly ADMIN_EMAILS; value is plain emails (no KEY=value);
# enable for Production (and Preview if you use it). After deploy, POST /api/auth/login
# returns JSON { role } — should be ADMIN when the allowlist matches.
# ADMIN_EMAILS=you@example.com,cofounder@example.com

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PDF export (admin API + local script)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Base URL headless Chrome loads when generating PDFs. Defaults to VERCEL_URL on
# Vercel, or http://localhost:3002 locally. The app must be reachable at this URL.
# PDF_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3002
#
# Optional bearer token for /api/pdf, /api/pdf/site, and /api/pdf/site/full when not signed in as admin.
# PDF_EXPORT_SECRET=your-long-random-secret

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Stripe (cook listing subscription)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Create a monthly recurring Price in Stripe Dashboard for "Munch Kitchen Listing",
# then set STRIPE_LISTING_PRICE_ID to that price ID (price_...).
#
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_...
# NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_...
# STRIPE_LISTING_PRICE_ID=price_...
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_...
#
# Optional platform fee on food orders (percent kept by Munch). Example: 10 = 10%
# STRIPE_PLATFORM_FEE_PERCENT=10
#
# Stripe Connect: enable Connect in Dashboard → Settings → Connect.
# Cook dashboard → "Connect with Stripe" runs Express onboarding.
# Food checkout uses destination charges: customer pays, cook receives transfer minus fee.
#
# Webhook events to enable: checkout.session.completed, checkout.session.expired,
# account.updated, customer.subscription.*, invoice.payment_failed
# Demo cook (after seed): cook@munch.com / demo1234 — assign COOK role + kitchen in admin.
# DEMO_COOK_PASSWORD defaults to demo1234 (override with DEMO_COOK_PASSWORD).

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Geocoding (Nominatim / OpenStreetMap)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Required for production geocoding per OSM usage policy (identify your app).
# NOMINATIM_USER_AGENT=MunchWebApp/1.0 (contact you@example.com)
